# Design authority

`PRODUCT.md` and `DESIGN.md` at the repository root are the design and product authority. Read them
before any UI, CSS, layout, component, copy or state-design work. This rule does not restate them.

## Global platform: The Exchange Desk

Commodity Chain is a multi-protocol regulated-market console. The global shell direction is **The
Exchange Desk**: dark navy navigation rail, light operational work surface, Golos Text with
kk/ru/en support, `#0A4F8C` as the single action colour, restrained colour, minimal shadow, 4–6px
radii, tables and ledgers over decorative card grids.

Quality references are KASE, Addepar and institutional capital-markets workstations. No generic AI
aesthetics, no crypto neon, no decorative card proliferation.

## Protocol context boundary

Field to Finance is one protocol on Commodity Chain, not the platform.

- Harvest Capital (`.cursor/skills/harvest-capital-ui/SKILL.md`) is an **optional Field to Finance
  contextual layer only**. Use it only when a task explicitly calls for F2F-specific visual
  treatment.
- Harvest Capital must never define the global Commodity Chain shell.
- Agriculture imagery and language must never be applied to Water, Music Rights, Gaming Assets or
  any future protocol.
- Neither this rule nor that skill overrides `PRODUCT.md` or `DESIGN.md`.

## Scope

Do not perform a broad visual redesign as a side effect of a feature change. Do not add a parallel
UI tree; the shell is restyled in place when that work is scheduled.
